Theorem IA-1 + IA-7: Backward-dataflow soundness + convergence

  Preconditions:
    - Function F with a single block B = [i_1; i_2; ...; i_n; return v]
    - AimsStateMap per Annex E §AIMS §7 (block_entry_states +
      block_exit_states)
    - Direction is BACKWARD per Annex E §AIMS IA-1
    - alt_join is the lattice join (max) per Annex E §AIMS.3
    - seq_add is the QTT additive composition per Annex E §AIMS.3
    - CHAIN_HEIGHT = 16 per Annex E §AIMS.8 (Access(1) +
      Consumption(3) + Cardinality(2) + Uniqueness(2) + Locality(4) +
      Shape(1) + Effect(3))

  Soundness property:
    The backward analysis converges to an AimsStateMap satisfying:
      (1) For every variable v, v's exit state at any program point p
          is the alt_join of v's entry states at p's successors.
      (2) Each backward transfer step is monotone per L-6 across
          the dimension subset it touches (Cardinality + Consumption
          via seq_add; Locality via max).
      (3) Convergence is reached in at most
          CHAIN_HEIGHT * |variables| * |blocks| iterations;
          for this synthetic 1-block F, |blocks| = 1, so the bound
          is 16 * |variables|.

  Proof obligation:
    Structural induction on the backward walk over B's instructions
    (in REVERSE order from terminator to entry):
      Base case: terminator (Return v).
        IA-3 seeds exit state from TF-11a Return demand: (v, 1, L)
        per the Return row of the terminator-demand table.
      Inductive step: instruction i_k.
        Assume entry state at position k+1 is sound.
        Apply IA-5 step (1) (alias transfer via seq_add) on aliasing
        defs (Let Var, Project, Select, Construct, Reuse,
        CollectionReuse, PartialApply, Set with TF-13 Construct
        rule);
        apply IA-5 step (2) (TF-11 backward demand) for operand
        consumption;
        remove the defined variable from the entry-state map.
        Monotonicity (L-6) preserved per dimension: Cardinality +
        Consumption via seq_add (commutative, monotone on QTT
        carriers); Locality via max (monotone on totally-ordered
        carrier).

    Convergence (IA-7):
      The state lattice has finite height
        CHAIN_HEIGHT = 16 per dimension sum;
      each variable's state ascends monotonically across iterations;
      total ascent <= CHAIN_HEIGHT * |variables| * |blocks|;
      for this 1-block F: at most 16 * |variables| iterations.

    Case analysis on instruction shape (per the IA-5 step (1)
    by-instruction-type table):
      Let { Var(v) } (transparent alias): demand transfers to v via
        seq_add on Cardinality + Consumption, max on Locality.
      Project (borrow, NOT alias): TF-14 propagation
        (src.cardinality := seq_add(src.cardinality, dst.cardinality);
         src.locality := max(src.locality, dst.locality);
         src.consumption := seq_add(src.consumption, A)).
      Construct (aggregate builder): destination's LOCALITY transfers
        to args (arg.locality := max); args ALWAYS promoted to
        access := O.
      All other instructions: no alias transfer; TF-11 direct demand
        only.

    Permutation-invariance (IA-9): N-ary alt_join at CFG merges is
      permutation-invariant per L-1 + L-2 (commutativity +
      associativity); fold order over successor states does not
      affect the result.

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (IA-1 backward walk + IA-5 alias-transfer
                            inductive step)
      fixpoint (IA-7 chain-height-bounded convergence)
      case_analysis (per-instruction-type IA-5 step (1) enumeration +
                     IA-9 N-ary join permutation-invariance discharge)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: IA-shape scaffold-time; engine implementation pending
